Z||000000||Philphine||08-05-2001||11:39 AM||||<BR>stopped at a nearby burger joint last night and when i started my car ('87 coupe) the battery light came on and i read 12v on an add on guage in the car. stayed on about 30 sec. then went out about 15sec. then came on and stayed on. i only had a couple of blocks to go so i turned off everything but headlights and drove home. stayed at 12v.<P>this morning i'm under the hood (trunk? trood? hunk?) looking for a loose connection and finding none. start the car and the light is on. check wiring while it's running to see if i can get some reaction from moving wires while it runs but it stayed on. got in the car and started to load it down by turning on everything. it dropped down to 9v for a couple secs then the light went out and i was reading 13-14v again. <P>i'm guessing the regulator part of my alt. might be going. i'm going to go by autozone after i post this to try and get it checked, but if the lights not on when they do it they may not see anything. <P>i have noticed too that my stereo will blip along with the voltmeter kicking recently so i'm still wondering about a bad connection somewhere but i don't know where yet. seems like i would have blown a fuse or a fusible link if so. <P>sorry this got long but i was trying to give the best explanation i could to get the best answer offered. thanks for any help.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-05-2001||11:56 AM||||It does sound like the voltage regulator is bad in the alternator.It should put out at least 13 volts.If it were me, while at auto zone getting the alternator checked out I would pick one up. I'll bet that it  will prove to be defective any ways during the check.good luck ||||reg||1
